Consider this class:

public class Counter {
    private static int count = 0;
    private int id;

    public Counter() {
        count++;
        id = count;
    }

    public int getId() {
        return id;
    }
}

If three Counter objects are created in this order — c1, c2, c3 — what does c3.getId() return?

public class Bank {
    private static double totalDeposits = 0;

    public static void deposit(double amt) {
        totalDeposits += amt;
    }

    public static double getTotal() {
        return totalDeposits;
    }
}

In client code, Bank.deposit(100) is called, then Bank.deposit(50) is called. What does Bank.getTotal() return?
